<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">[Game Programming Syllabus Mapping](#30-game-programming-syllabus-mapping)</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">1. Title</h2>
<strong>Tappy Bird: Skybound Challenge</strong>  
A Multistage 2D Browser-Based Arcade Game demonstrating Computer Graphics, Kinematic Physics, and Game Engine Architecture.</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">2. Introduction</h2>
Video game programming synthesizes foundational computer science disciplines: linear algebra, coordinate transformations, numerical physics simulation, real-time input dispatching, audio synthesis, and graphics rendering pipelines. <strong>Tappy Bird: Skybound Challenge</strong> was engineered from the ground up using pure standard web technologies (HTML5 Canvas, Vanilla ECMAScript, and modern CSS) without third-party frameworks, paid APIs, or external game engines such as Unity or Phaser.</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">3. Problem Statement</h2>
Many introductory game development projects either rely too heavily on heavyweight third-party game engines (which abstract away essential mathematical and rendering concepts), or reduce the scope to a static, single-screen flappy clone devoid of progressive mechanics. The challenge for CA-2 is to engineer a multi-stage, mathematically rigorous, self-contained 2D game running offline in standard browsers that visibly demonstrates every topic of the Game Programming curriculum.</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">4. Game Concept</h2>
The player pilots a kinetic avian character through perilous skies segmented into three distinct levels of increasing difficulty. The player overcomes continuous gravitational acceleration through discrete flap impulses, timing vertical trajectory through advancing pipe obstacles. Each level introduces distinct environmental dynamics, varying physics parameters, oscillating structures, weather particle systems, and responsive obstacle behavior.</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">5. Objectives</h2>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Implement a real-time, deterministic 60 FPS game loop utilizing <code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">requestAnimationFrame()</code> with delta-time ($\Delta t$) clamping.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Develop a Newtonian physics system with position vectors, velocity vectors, and gravity Euler integration.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Construct transformation matrices (<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">translate</code>, <code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">rotate</code>, <code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">scale</code>) for velocity-based tilt orientation.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Implement rigorous Axis-Aligned Bounding Box (AABB) and Circle-to-Rectangle collision algorithms.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Create a 3-tier level progression system with distinct objectives, environmental themes, and dynamic obstacles.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Provide procedural, zero-dependency audio using the HTML5 Web Audio API to prevent CORS errors during offline evaluation.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Implement persistent data storage using browser <code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">localStorage</code> for high scores and level unlocks.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">6. Technologies Used</h2>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>HTML5 Canvas 2D Context:</strong> Low-level immediate mode graphics rendering.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Vanilla JavaScript (ES6+):</strong> Object-oriented classes, state machines, and mathematical calculations.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Modern CSS3:</strong> Glassmorphic UI overlays, typography, flexbox/grid layout, and arcade glow effects.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>HTML5 Web Audio API:</strong> Procedural mathematical frequency synthesis for real-time sound effects.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Browser LocalStorage API:</strong> Client-side persistent key-value storage.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">7. Hardware/Software Requirements</h2>
<h3 style="color: #2563eb; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 13pt; margin-top: 12pt;">Software Requirements:</h3>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Any modern web browser (Google Chrome 90+, Mozilla Firefox 88+, Microsoft Edge 90+, Safari 14+).</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Text/Code editor (Antigravity IDE, Visual Studio Code, Sublime Text).</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">No web server or database required (operates natively via <code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">file://</code>).</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h3 style="color: #2563eb; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 13pt; margin-top: 12pt;">Hardware Requirements:</h3>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Processor:</strong> Dual-core 1.6 GHz or higher.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>RAM:</strong> 2 GB minimum (4 GB recommended).</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Display Resolution:</strong> Minimum $800 \times 600$ (optimized for $480 \times 640$ viewport).</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Input:</strong> Keyboard and Mouse / Touchpad / Touchscreen.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">8. Game Controls</h2>
| Action | Primary Input | Secondary / Touch | Function |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| <strong>Flap Wings</strong> | <code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">SPACE</code> | Mouse Left Click / Screen Tap | Imparts upward velocity impulse vector |
| <strong>Pause / Resume</strong> | <code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">P</code> | Top HUD ⏸ Button | Toggles active physics and object updates |
| <strong>Back / Menu</strong> | <code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">ESC</code> | UI On-screen Buttons | Navigates back from sub-menus |
| <strong>Mute Sound</strong> | <code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">M</code> | Top HUD 🔊 Button | Toggles Web Audio master gain state |</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">9. Gameplay</h2>
The player begins at the Main Menu with options to start playing, select unlocked stages, or view flight instructions. Upon starting:
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">The bird spawns at $(x = 110, y = 260)$.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Gravity continuously pulls the bird downward along the positive Y Cartesian axis.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">The player flaps to maintain altitude and pass through gaps between vertical pipes.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Successfully crossing a pipe's horizontal boundary increments the stage score.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Reaching the stage target score clears the level and unlocks the subsequent stage.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Colliding with a pipe, the ground, or the sky ceiling triggers an immediate Game Over with a retry option.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">10. Game Architecture</h2>
The codebase adheres to the Single Responsibility Principle (SRP) through modular ES6 classes:
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">Game</code>: Central coordinator, state machine, and <code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">requestAnimationFrame</code> loop.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">Bird</code>: Avatar kinematics, Euler integration, tilt rotation, and wing animation.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">Obstacle</code>: Base static pipe pair class.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">MovingObstacle</code>: Subclass with harmonic vertical oscillation ($A \sin(\omega t)$).</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">AIObstacle</code>: Subclass with predictive altitude-tracking gap behavior.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">CollisionSystem</code>: Circle-AABB and boundary intersection calculations.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">LevelManager</code>: Configurations for 3 stages, weather engines (rain, lightning, clouds, stars).</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">ScoreManager</code>: Current score, target goals, campaign tracking, and <code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">localStorage</code>.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">InputManager</code>: HID keyboard, mouse, and touch listener registry with debounce protection.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">UIManager</code>: DOM overlay transitions, HUD updates, modal display.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">AudioManager</code>: Web Audio API sound synthesizer.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">11. Game Loop</h2>
The application implements an industry-standard game loop pattern:
``<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Calculate Delta Time: dt = (currentTime - lastTime) / 1000</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Clamp Delta Time: dt = min(dt, 0.08)</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Process Inputs: Check keyboard and pointer flags</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Update World Objects: bird.update(dt), obstacle.update(dt), environment.update(dt)</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Detect Collisions: CollisionSystem.checkBirdObstacle(bird, obs)</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Check Scoring & Objectives: bird.x > obs.x + obs.width</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Clear Canvas: ctx.clearRect(0, 0, width, height)</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Render Frame: Background -> Obstacles -> Bird -> HUD Overlays</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Schedule Next Frame: requestAnimationFrame(gameLoop)</li>
</code>`<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;"></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">12. Level 1 — "Training Sky"</h2>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Easy</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Target Score:</strong> 10 points</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Gravity Acceleration:</strong> $800 \text{ px/s}^2$</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Flap Impulse:</strong> $320 \text{ px/s}$</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Horizontal Speed:</strong> $155 \text{ px/s}$</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Pipe Gap:</strong> $165 \text{ px}$</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Obstacle Configuration:</strong> 100% static pipe pairs.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Visual Atmosphere:</strong> Bright daylight sky gradient, drifting cumulus clouds, peaceful sunny horizon.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Objective:</strong> Introduce basic controls and familiarize player with timing and momentum.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">13. Level 2 — "Storm Sky"</h2>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Medium</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Target Score:</strong> 15 points</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Gravity Acceleration:</strong> $920 \text{ px/s}^2$</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Flap Impulse:</strong> $345 \text{ px/s}$</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Horizontal Speed:</strong> $210 \text{ px/s}$</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Pipe Gap:</strong> $140 \text{ px}$</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Obstacle Configuration:</strong> 50% vertical moving obstacles oscillating sinusoidally ($y = y_0 + 45\sin(2.2t)$).</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Visual Atmosphere:</strong> Tempest slate background, active rain particle system (70 streaks with wind slant), dynamic lightning flashes.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Objective:</strong> Challenge player reflexes against moving targets and visual distractions.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">14. Level 3 — "Nightmare Sky"</h2>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Hard</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Target Score:</strong> 20 points</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Gravity Acceleration:</strong> $1050 \text{ px/s}^2$</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Flap Impulse:</strong> $375 \text{ px/s}$</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Horizontal Speed:</strong> $260 \text{ px/s}$</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Pipe Gap:</strong> $120 \text{ px}$</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Obstacle Configuration:</strong> Oscillating pipes and AI-inspired adaptive tracking obstacles.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Visual Atmosphere:</strong> Deep cosmic night sky, parallax twinkling starfield, crescent moon, neon obsidian pipes.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Objective:</strong> Test master-level precision flight under high gravity and narrow clearances.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">15. Mathematics/Graphics Concepts Used</h2>
The engine applies foundational linear algebra and calculus principles:
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Position Vectors:</strong> $\vec{r} = (x, y)$</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Velocity Vectors:</strong> $\vec{v} = (v_x, v_y)$</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Vector Addition:</strong> $\vec{r}_{t+\Delta t} = \vec{r}_t + \vec{v}\Delta t$</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Harmonic Motion:</strong> $y(t) = y_{\text{base}} + A \sin(\omega t + \phi)$</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Rotation Matrix:</strong> 2D Cartesian plane rotation about the origin.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Pythagorean Distance Optimization:</strong> Testing squared Euclidean distance $(d^2 \le r^2)$ to avoid expensive square root operations.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">16. Vectors</h2>
A vector in 2D space represents magnitude and direction:
$$\vec{v} = \begin{bmatrix} v_x \\ v_y \end{bmatrix}$$
In our simulation, gravity is a constant acceleration vector directed downwards: $\vec{g} = (0, g)$.
Flapping exerts an instantaneous impulse vector directed upwards: $\vec{J} = (0, -F_{\text{flap}})$.</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">17. Coordinate System</h2>
The game operates in standard 2D Screen Cartesian space:
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Origin $(0, 0)$:</strong> Upper-left corner of the HTML5 Canvas.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>X-Axis:</strong> Extends horizontally to the right ($+X$).</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Y-Axis:</strong> Extends vertically downward ($+Y$).</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Playable World Dimensions:</strong> $480 \text{ px (Width)} \times 640 \text{ px (Height)}$.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Ground Datum:</strong> Positioned at $y = 580 \text{ px}$.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">18. Transformations</h2>
Affine transformations are implemented using Canvas context transformation stack:
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"></code>ctx.save()<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">: Preserves previous transformation state.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"></code>ctx.translate(bird.x, bird.y)<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">: Shifts origin to bird center.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"></code>ctx.rotate(theta)<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">: Rotates plane by angle $\theta$ proportional to vertical velocity:</li>
   $$\theta = \text{clamp}\left(\frac{v_y}{500} \times 1.2, -0.38 \text{ rad}, +1.22 \text{ rad}\right)$$
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"></code>ctx.restore()<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">: Restores global coordinate space for subsequent entities.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">19. Physics</h2>
Numerical physics simulation utilizes First-Order Semi-Implicit Euler Integration:
$$v_y(t + \Delta t) = v_y(t) + g \cdot \Delta t$$
$$y(t + \Delta t) = y(t) + v_y(t + \Delta t) \cdot \Delta t$$
To prevent physics tunneling through obstacles during lag spikes, $\Delta t$ is capped at $0.08 \text{ s}$.</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">20. Collision Detection</h2>
The collision subsystem employs Circle-to-AABB (Axis-Aligned Bounding Box) testing:
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Given a bird circle with center $(c_x, c_y)$ and radius $r$, and a pipe rectangle $[x_1, y_1, x_2, y_2]$:</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Find the closest point $(p_x, p_y)$ on the rectangle to the circle:</li>
   $$p_x = \max(x_1, \min(c_x, x_2))$$
   $$p_y = \max(y_1, \min(c_y, y_2))$$
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Compute distance squared: $d^2 = (c_x - p_x)^2 + (c_y - p_y)^2$</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">If $d^2 \le r^2$, an intersection exists.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">21. Rendering</h2>
Rendering employs immediate mode 2D Canvas rendering:
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Radial and linear gradients create lighting and depth on pipes, sky, and character.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Dual-pass rendering ensures background scenery is drawn before interactive entities and UI overlays.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Double buffering is handled natively by </code>requestAnimationFrame<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;"> before blitting to display hardware.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">22. Animation</h2>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Wing Flapping:</strong> Evaluates $\sin(\text{phase})$ to dynamically vary ellipse radii and vertical offsets.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Particle Systems:</strong> Feather and smoke trail particles spawn on flap impulse with velocity, decay, and alpha fading.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Environmental Parallax:</strong> Clouds and ground stripes scroll horizontally proportional to stage velocity.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">23. Game Engine Concepts</h2>
The project demonstrates core structural game engine design patterns:
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>State Machine Pattern:</strong> Regulates transitions between </code>MENU<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">, </code>PLAYING<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">, </code>PAUSED<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">, </code>LEVEL_COMPLETE<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">, </code>GAME_OVER<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">, and </code>VICTORY<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Component Separation:</strong> Rendering, input processing, and physics are decoupled into dedicated classes.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Object Pooling / Garbage Cleanup:</strong> Offscreen obstacles are pruned using </code>splice<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;"> to prevent memory leaks.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">24. Input Handling</h2>
The </code>InputManager<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;"> class intercepts Human Interface Device (HID) events:
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Listens to </code>keydown<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">, </code>keyup<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">, and </code>pointerdown<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Enforces key release before re-triggering flap impulses to prevent holding the spacebar to hover.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Normalizes mouse clicks and mobile touch events onto a unified canvas input handler.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">25. UI Management</h2>
User interface layers are organized into glassmorphic DOM modals floating over the game canvas:
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">CSS </code>backdrop-filter: blur(12px)<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;"> provides modern aesthetics.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Reactive HUD displaying stage number, live score, target goal, and an animated progress bar.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Responsive feedback dialogs for Stage Clear, Game Over, Pause, and Grand Victory.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">26. Testing</h2>
Comprehensive functional and boundary testing was performed:
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Frame Rate Stability:</strong> Maintained a consistent 60 FPS across extended playthroughs.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Edge Collisions:</strong> Verified that grazing pipe corners, flying into the ceiling, or touching the ground immediately registers collision.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>State Resets:</strong> Confirmed that retrying resets velocity, positions, and timers without residual velocity.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Storage Persistence:</strong> High score and stage unlock flags persist after refreshing the browser.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Web Audio Compatibility:</strong> Verified that sound plays cleanly across Chrome, Edge, and Firefox without CORS blocking.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">27. Results</h2>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">A completely functional, 3-level playable 2D game running in all major browsers.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">100% offline functionality without any build step, npm dependency, or external server.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Clear visual distinction and graduated difficulty between Training Sky, Storm Sky, and Nightmare Sky.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">28. Future Scope</h2>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Addition of power-ups (e.g., invincibility shield, speed boost, coin magnets).</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Sprite sheet asset importing with texture atlas animations.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Online leaderboard synchronization using WebSocket services.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;">Procedurally generated infinite survival mode following Stage 3 completion.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">29. Conclusion</h2>
"Tappy Bird: Skybound Challenge" successfully fulfills all requirements for the CA-2 Game Programming evaluation. By writing pure vanilla JavaScript and HTML5 Canvas code without high-level engines, the project clearly demonstrates low-level mastery of coordinate spaces, vector mathematics, kinematic physics, collision algorithms, state machines, and real-time rendering pipelines.</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;">---</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h2 style="color: #1d4ed8; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 18pt;">30. Game Programming Syllabus Mapping</h2></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h3 style="color: #2563eb; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 13pt; margin-top: 12pt;">Unit I: Mathematics & Transformations</h3>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Cartesian Coordinate System & XY Plane:</strong> Canvas coordinate space ($X$ right, $Y$ down) implemented in </code>bird.js<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;"> and </code>game.js<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Vectors & Kinematics:</strong> Position $\vec{r}$ and velocity $\vec{v}$ vectors integrated with gravity $\vec{g}$.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Transformations (Translation, Rotation, Scaling):</strong> </code>ctx.translate()<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;"> and </code>ctx.rotate()<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;"> dynamically tilting the bird based on instantaneous vertical velocity.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Geometric Shapes:</strong> Rectangles (pipes, ground), circles (bird, particles, sun, moon), and polygons (beak, crest) drawn via Canvas 2D API paths.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h3 style="color: #2563eb; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 13pt; margin-top: 12pt;">Unit II: Engine Architecture & Pipelines</h3>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>CPU vs GPU Concept:</strong> JavaScript execution on CPU; rasterization and alpha compositing hardware-accelerated by GPU via Canvas 2D context.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Game Loop & Delta Time:</strong> </code>requestAnimationFrame()<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;"> with clamped $\Delta t$ ensuring consistent physics independent of display refresh rate (60Hz vs 144Hz).</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Collision Detection:</strong> Circle-to-AABB bounding box intersection separated cleanly in </code>collision.js<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Input (HID) Processing:</strong> Keyboard, mouse, and touch events mapped through </code>inputManager.js<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>UI & State Management:</strong> Decoupled HTML/CSS overlay screens and state machine in </code>uiManager.js<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;"> and </code>game.js<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">.</li></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 8pt;"><h3 style="color: #2563eb; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 13pt; margin-top: 12pt;">Unit III: 2D Game Development & AI</h3>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Level Progression:</strong> 3 distinct stages with parameterized configurations in </code>levelManager.js<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Particle Systems & Animation:</strong> Procedural wing flap oscillation, weather effects (rain, lightning, clouds, stars), and feather trail particles.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Introduction to Game AI:</strong> Dynamic obstacle in Level 3 (</code>AIObstacle<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;"> in </code>obstacle.js<code style="background-color: #f1f5f9; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10pt; padding: 2px 4px;">) that tracks player altitude to create an adaptive gameplay hazard.</li>
<li style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 4px;"><strong>Audio Synthesis:</strong> Real-time Web Audio API procedural sound synthesis in </code>audioManager.js`.</li>
</p>
    </body>
    </html>
  